description:
What: Call TantivySearchIndex::index_article after successful POST in run_post_pipeline.

Algorithm:
1. In crates/reader/src/session/lifecycle.rs, in run_post_pipeline(), after the overview_store.insert() call (currently last step before returning 240):
   if let Some(idx) = &stores.search_index {
       let body_text = String::from_utf8_lossy(body_bytes);
       for (group_name, article_number) in &assignments {
           if let Err(e) = idx.index_article(
               &message_id,
               group_name,
               *article_number,
               &overview.subject,
               &overview.from,
               &overview.date,
               body_bytes,
           ).await {
               tracing::warn!(message_id = %message_id, error = %e, "search index failed, article still accepted");
           }
       }
       // Commit after each article (simple approach; can be batched later)
       if let Err(e) = idx.commit().await {
           tracing::warn!(error = %e, "search index commit failed");
       }
   }

2. Ensure this code is AFTER the 240 response would be sent — actually: it's before, but it's infallible from the POST response perspective. Even if indexing fails, POST returns 240.

3. Similarly add indexing hook to the IHAVE/TAKETHIS pipeline (in transit crate or reader IHAVE handler) — check which file handles IHAVE in the reader crate. If reader has its own IHAVE handler, add the same hook.

Defensive rules:
- NEVER reject a POST due to indexing failure. Log warning and return 240 anyway.
- NEVER log message_id or body content at ERROR level. Use warn! or debug! only.
- The hook is best-effort. If stores.search_index is None, skip silently.
- If assignments is empty, no indexing is attempted.
